			<div class="content" id="post-content-4477262">
									

<p>Hey! Thanks for the feedback, and I'm happy you enjoyed the article. I'm happy to adress some of this as best I can, but as you said yourself, this is a bit hard to describe in words. I'll try to go through line by line.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Collapsible&nbsp;for&nbsp;convenience</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">:)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The reason the anomaly is Safe is us really trying to lean into it as a containment class and a containment class only. We tried to allude to it in the article a bit, but it's not that just any artificial consciousness could stumble into the anomaly. It's things that are wrong or unhinged in some way. MARDUK.AIC was infected with a memetic hazard that it got from Foundation duties, the unknown was a pattern screamer (big reveal), and the third was made of a CotBG hive mind. Also it would require that consciousness to be powerful enough to enter the Noosphere in the first place. If you can't chuck yourself into the Noosphere using anomalous science, this thing can't really effect you.</p>
<p>I definitely understand confusion regarding the first sentence, because it was literally the first sentence that was written of this. &quot;Artistic constructohazard&quot; is a fancy way of describing what the anomaly does. It takes artistic concepts and uses them in physical constructions. It's biologically contained in the Noosphere because only unhinged technology can access it without assistance. Yes, a person could just physically enter the Noosphere through a Monolith, but that would first require a Monolith to be constructed and accessible. The three Monoliths in the log through are the only ones that were able to reach the Monolith stage, and its only because they were fast enough.</p>
<p>As for the confusion regarding what is affected, I think this is the best way to put it. The concepts that are mainly affected are ones that &quot;make up&quot; the person and their idea of creativity. 5000 wouldn't be able to spread to you because you aren't in the Noosphere.</p>
<p>Yes, this thing could cause some serious damage. But for the efforts of containment, there's not much you need to do. It's not like everyday people can shoot their consciousness into the Noosphere.</p>
<p>Hope this helped clear up things in one way or another!</p>
</div>
